{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1478263382,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxODczMjM5OTI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1093","origin":"github"},"title":"update --upgrade should enable possibly added new autoenabled special remotes","message":"ATM, if there is a new special remote was added/autoenabled on remote end, `git annex merge` does not activate it.  @joeyh -- do you think it should be done on git-annex side, or we should do it on ours ?\nRelevant earlier discussion:  https://git-annex.branchable.com/todo/autoenable__61__true_for_special_remotes/\nthis happens now to openfmri datasets, which (actually by mistake) got public URLs assigned to datalad remote (instead of standard web)... but if we `git annex merge`, it doesn't get autoactivated as if when we do a fresh clone.  As a workaround I could add 'git annex init' call to `update --merge` invocation, which should then re-enable all those remotes, but ideally I think there could be a logic during `git annex merge`, tracking what additional remotes were added  and autoenabling those which have autoenable=True.","files":null}]}